# =====================================================
# Claude Code (default-deny: local state ignored, shared assets opted in)
# =====================================================
# `.claude/*` excludes the *contents*, not the directory itself. That distinction
# matters: excluding `.claude/` outright would stop git descending into it, and a
# later `!.claude/...` negation would silently have no effect (see gitignore(5),
# "It is not possible to re-include a file if a parent directory is excluded").
# Verified empirically before choosing this form. New files the tool writes here
# are ignored by default; anything meant to be versioned is opted in below.

.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/

# =====================================================
# Private sanitization legend (placeholders -> real values, NEVER COMMIT)
# =====================================================

SANITIZATION-LEGEND.local.md
*.local.md
